 "texts": [
  {
   "title": "Source",
   "pos": [
    0,
    440
   ],
   "text": "Drawn from ElectroSmash's \"MXR Dyna Comp Analysis\" (schematic and parts\nlist, part numbers as there; TR1 is its \"Rtrimmer\", VR1 and VR2 its RV1 and RV2).\nhttps://www.electrosmash.com/mxr-dyna-comp-analysis"
  }
 ],
 "notes": {
  "part:Q1": "Input buffer: an emitter follower biased from VB (2.54 V) through R2.",
  "part:U1": "The OTA: its gain is set by the current into IABC (pin 5). More current, more gain; the envelope detector takes current away as the signal gets louder.",
  "part:TR1": "Balance trimmer: sets the + input against the - input so the output's DC doesn't move as the gain changes (no thump on each note).",
  "part:Q2": "Phase splitter: the same signal, inverted at the collector and not at the emitter, so the envelope detector sees both halves of the wave. The output is taken from the emitter.",
  "part:Q3": "Q3 and Q4 are off at rest; on the signal's peaks they pull C8 down, each on its own half of the wave.",
  "part:C8": "Holds the envelope: R13 charges it back up slowly after a note (the release), Q3 and Q4 discharge it quickly (the attack).",
  "part:Q5": "Follows C8 and drives the OTA's bias current through R17 and Sensitivity.",
